repository-code: "https://github.com/ReZaAdineH/UTIOM"
url: "https://utiom.de"
abstract: >-
  The UTIOM Framework (Unified Threat-Informed Operations Model) is a
  lifecycle operating framework for Security Operations and Incident
  Response.
  It unifies management intent, engineering discipline and operational
  execution into a single coherent, measurable system built around
  real adversary behaviour. The model spans seven phases across three
  pillars — Leadership and governance (Vision, Strategy, Crown Jewels),
  Engineering and enablement (Threat Visibility, Threat Detection), and
  Operations and analysis (Response, Continuous Improvement). It
  operationalises rather than replaces established standards including
  NIST CSF 2.0, SOC-CMM, DORA and MITRE ATT&CK.
